<title>JAPAN: Oki Electric's 96/97 profit seen falling sharply.</title>
<headline>Oki Electric's 96/97 profit seen falling sharply.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oki Electric Industry Co Ltd's parent current profit in the year to March 31, 1997, is expected to fall 79 percent from a year ago to about 10 billion yen, due to the sluggish semiconductor market, Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported.</p>
<p>The company earlier this year said its 1996/97 parent current profit would be about 20 billion yen.</p>
<p>A company spokesman was not immediately available for comment.</p>
